WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
The World Bank sorts the
world's countries by income,

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.850
and gives each one a single label.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.250
Niger and Rwanda: low income.

4
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.770
The UK, Japan and Qatar: high income.

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.990
India is lower-middle income.

6
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.670
China is upper-middle.

7
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.330
One label each, for the whole country.

8
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.810
But a country is not one place.

9
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.930
So can one word really
tell you how rich it is?

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.890
In this mission, you'll read
the World Bank's income map,

11
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.630
and spot its global pattern.

12
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.090
Then you'll test what a country's
income label can tell you,

13
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.110
and what it can't.

14
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: find out whether one
label can describe a whole country.
